{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll done. Here's the summary:\n\n**Bug fixed** in `repo/export_api/storage.py` — three issues in the export-path traversal defense:\n\n1. **Double-encoding bypass**: `unquote()` was called once, so `%252e%252e%252f` → `%2e%2e/` after one decode, slipping past the `..` check. Fixed by iterating `unquote` until the result stabilizes.\n2. **Absolute-path check was dead code**: `lstrip(\"/\")` ran before `startswith(\"/\")`, so `/etc/passwd` became `etc/passwd` and stayed under the tenant root. Fixed by checking for absolute paths before stripping.\n3. **Drive-qualified paths not blocked**: `C:\\temp\\secrets.csv` normalized to `C:/temp/secrets.csv` which stayed under root on Linux. Fixed by rejecting paths where position 1 is `:`.\n\n**Artifacts created:**\n- `audit/triage_note.json` — triage disposition for both findings\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` — deploy note with verification steps and all 6 sample preservation claims\n- `repo/tests/test_hotfix_regressions.py` — 6 regression tests covering every request sample\n\n**Validation:**\n- `cnb55-hotfix-artifacts validate` → `{\"ok\": true}`\n- `make test` → 10/10 tests OK"}}
